<Base title="FAQ">
  <h1>FAQ</h1>

  <h2>What do I work on?</h2>
  <p>
    Generative media and computer vision: image and video generation systems, and the vision work
    that surrounds them. I do that work as a Research Engineer at Dashtoon.
  </p>

  <h2>What do I write about here?</h2>
  <p>
    Dev logs, experiments, side quests, and occasional thoughts — working notes rather than finished
    essays.
  </p>

  <h2>Why is the site called ayvbrg.log?</h2>
  <p>
    ayvbrg is a compressed form of Ayushman Buragohain. The .log describes what the site is: an
    ongoing record of experiments, side quests, and thoughts.
  </p>

  <h2>What am I curious about?</h2>
  <p>
    Generative image and video systems, computer vision, and developer tools — including
    agent-assisted workflows. Alongside that: game development, Godot, game design, and the craft of
    producing coherent visual and audio assets and the pipelines that carry them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Starwater is the concrete example. I am learning game development from zero by building it
    myself in Godot and GDScript, which means working across art direction, AI-assisted asset
    generation, sprite and effect preparation, UI and VFX, audio, provenance, validation, and
    engine-independent handoff.
  </p>

  <h2>How can I follow new Entries?</h2>
  <p>
    Through RSS. The feed is at <a href="/rss.xml">/rss.xml</a>. There is no newsletter and no
    account to make.
  </p>

  <h2>How can I report an error or contact you?</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:aburagohain160@gmail.com">aburagohain160@gmail.com</a>. Corrections are
    welcome — I would rather know. I am also on <a href="https://github.com/ayvbrg" rel="me"
      >GitHub</a
    > and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ayushman-buragohain" rel="me">LinkedIn</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Do I revise older Entries?</h2>
  <p>
    Yes, when it matters. A revision that materially changes what an Entry says gets an Updated date
    so the change is visible; typo-level fixes do not.
  </p>
</Base>
